{
  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_021: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat → acc 0.527), the most critical uncertainty is whether the low performance stems from the multimodal fusion, the RNA representation, or the inherent difficulty of the task. Config_028 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_021: it removes the RNA modality while keeping the image encoder (resnet50) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical. If image-only matches or exceeds 0.527, the PCA-RNA branch is not contributing and we should focus on image encoder quality or multiprofile. If image-only is substantially lower, the multimodal combination is genuinely adding signal and we should explore better RNA encoders or fusion strategies. This baseline is foundational for interpreting all future multimodal results and is the highest-information experiment given the sparse evidence."
}

